      "documentConcept": "Salesforce Case alert rule versioning and activation semantics",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:3f7423d4d26b77ed4fab9978b6c5a5e917a2475f87f97474f091cab74f0d657e",
      "text": "Flow-based Case alerts have a version activation boundary: a new active version replaces the previous one for new work, while running interviews keep their starting version. Production deployment can leave a Flow inactive, and cleanup must respect paused interviews. Native Case escalation rules have a separate activation mechanism that replaces the existing active escalation rule. The claims distinguish documented platform behavior from vendor recommendations for release traceability and rollback. These sources do not establish a version-selection policy for an external Pub/Sub alert evaluator.",
